Cryogenic Engineering — M. D. Atrey, IIT Bombay (@gas-cryogenic-course: 0, is #reference, #part-of @gas-sources) { r_65F71B6VYE8297NF8ZN1D3S783
M. D. Atrey, IIT Bombay. *Cryogenic Engineering*, NPTEL course 112101004. [Official course](https://nptel.ac.in/courses/112101004), [complete syllabus](https://archive.nptel.ac.in/content/syllabus_pdf/112101004.pdf), [instructor's course description](https://www.me.iitb.ac.in/~matrey/nptel.html).

Work through the complete public lecture sequence, using the shared thermal and mathematical foundations when a derivation needs them. Gas properties, low-temperature materials, liquefaction, refrigeration and separation lead into cryocoolers, insulation, vacuum, instrumentation, storage/transfer and cryostat design. Reconstruct the cycle and separation balances, then examine how nonideal equipment changes them.

The instructor identifies 42 lectures. His description and the full two-page syllabus were inspected on 30 October 2026. Individual lecture playback, all exercises and historical download links were not independently verified. The instructor's link labelled lecture notes points to syllabus material; do not describe it as a complete written textbook.

Free educational access is distinct from redistribution rights and paid certification. Preserve the course/component notices. Commercial books listed in its bibliography are not supplied by the course links. Keep all media external.

